# ReviewBoost mobile — environment
#
# Copy to `.env` for local development. `.env*.local` is gitignored.
#
# Only three variables exist, and all are EXPO_PUBLIC_*. Anything prefixed
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ is inlined into the compiled JS bundle and ships to every
# device, so it is NOT a secret. The three below are safe to expose:
#   - the Supabase URL is public,
#   - the anon (publishable) key grants nothing on its own — every table
#     denies `anon`, and what a signed-in session may read is decided by
#     Row Level Security in the database,
#   - the API URL is just the public web origin.
#
# NEVER add any of these to the mobile app or to EXPO_PUBLIC_* anywhere —
# they would leak to every device:
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, Stripe secret keys (sk_*), the customer-note
#   encryption key, the token-digest key, or any other server-only secret.

# --- Local development (.env) -------------------------------------------
# Production Supabase project is zoyqikgqfqulwkihjbev.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://zoyqikgqfqulwkihjbev.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# The web app origin the mobile client calls. Production is the live domain.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://reviewboost.fit

# --- EAS builds (cloud) --------------------------------------------------
# `eas secret:create` is deprecated. Use EAS Environment Variables, which are
# scoped to the development / preview / production environments that each
# eas.json build profile is bound to via its "environment" field.
#
# URL and API_URL are also set inline in eas.json (non-secret defaults); the
# anon key is provided per environment so it never has to live in git:
#
#   eas env:create --environment production \
#     --name EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY \
#     --value <production anon key> --visibility plaintext --type string
#
#   # repeat for --environment preview and --environment development
#
# List / verify what a build will see:
#   eas env:list --environment production
#   eas env:get --environment production --name EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#
# `--visibility plaintext` is correct here precisely because EXPO_PUBLIC_*
# values are not secrets. Never store a server secret as an EAS env var and
# never give it an EXPO_PUBLIC_ name.
